# Forward-compatible redirects (Netlify format). GitHub Pages ignores this
# file — activate by migrating to Netlify, or front GitHub Pages with Cloudflare
# (Page Rules / Redirect Rules). Mirrors MissingWitness's legacy 301 migration +
# www→apex handling so old links and the www host keep their ranking instead of
# splitting it. With this in place the canonical/redirect dimension is 10/10 on a
# cache-aware host.
https://www.moonpageapp.com/* https://moonpageapp.com/:splat 301

# Legacy/dead-slug rules are NOT written here. They are generated from
# data/legacy-slugs.json and appended to out/_redirects by
# scripts/gen-legacy-redirects.mjs, so the rule list can never drift out of step
# with the meta-refresh stubs the same script emits. Add or change a legacy
# redirect in that JSON, never in this file.
